(FUN-05 — a function name is a bare single word or a single-quoted
 multi-word name (LANGUAGE.md:719, restated for the call site at :768).
 Both forms define and both forms call. The manual's wording pairs "bare"
 with "single word" and "single-quoted" with "multi-word", but the
 compiler also accepts a single-word name written SINGLE-QUOTED, at the
 definition and at the call — so the manual is narrower than the
 language. Nothing here is wrong; the rule to take from it is that a leaf
 must not treat "single-word names are never quoted" as a rule, because
 no rule says it.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox FUN-05.vox -o p && ./p
